[49m[38;5;10m+      1[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! Differential tests: C `libdriver.so` vs. Rust `libdriver.so`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! Both objects are loaded with `libloading` and every call goes through the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! `.so`'s exported symbol — the Rust functions are never called directly, so
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! the `#[no_mangle]` / `extern "C"` wrappers are part of what is tested.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! ## Why the harness controls the stack
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! `bad()` reads an uninitialized `char *` (CWE-457), so its output is a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! function of the caller's stack residue. Comparing the two libraries
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! meaningfully therefore requires *pinning* that residue: before every call the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! harness overwrites the stack region the callee will occupy with a chosen
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! pattern, and then calls the C and the Rust symbol from one identical call
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! site at one identical stack depth (`perform`, whose only difference between
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! the two runs is the runtime value of a function pointer).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! Two residue patterns are used:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! * `ResidueMode::Uniform` — every word gets the same 64-bit value, so the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!   *content* `bad()` emits is under test.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! * `ResidueMode::Indexed` — word *i* gets a pointer to the distinct string
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!   `slotNNNN` (NNNN = i), so the emitted label identifies *exactly which stack
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!   word the callee read*. This is what makes an offset mismatch between the C
