[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     962[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     }
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     963[0m:[38;5;10m[49m }
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     964[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     965[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// Row 26 — which stack word does the callee actually read? The residue is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     966[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// filled with 64 *distinct* pointers (`slot0000`..`slot0063`), so the emitted
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     967[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// label names the exact 8-byte offset. C and Rust must name the same one, for
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     968[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// `bad()` and for `driver(0)`, and the label must be stable across repeats.
