[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## How the CWE-457 read is made comparable
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `bad()` reads an uninitialized `char *`, so its output is a function of stack
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m residue — with an uncontrolled stack it is a coin flip driven by ASLR (measured:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ~50/50 between "prints nothing" and "prints library text", for *both* libraries).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Comparing that directly proves nothing.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `tests/differential.rs` therefore pins the residue: inline asm writes 64 chosen
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m words to `[rsp-512 .. rsp-8]` immediately before an indirect call, and the C and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the Rust symbol are then called from one identical call site at one identical
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m stack depth. Two patterns are used:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **uniform** — every word gets the same value, putting the *content* `bad()`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   emits under test;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **indexed** — word *i* points at the distinct string `slotNNNN`, so the bytes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   that come out name the exact stack word the callee read.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Under the indexed pattern the two libraries name the same word every time:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `bad()` reads `slot0060`, `driver(0)` reads `slot0056`. That is the check that
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m makes a frame-layout mismatch a failure rather than a coincidence.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Fixes made to the Rust side
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **The four functions were rewritten as `#[naked]` transcriptions of the C
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m build's disassembly.** The previous implementation used `MaybeUninit` slots plus
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m volatile accesses; that matched the C at `--release` but *not* in the `dev`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m profile, where `printLine`/`bad`/`good` grow from `sub $0x10,%rsp` to
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `0x90`/`0x70`/`0x80` and the slot `bad` reads moves ten words — a different
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m string reaches stdout. Since the frame geometry is observable through the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     64[0m:[38;5;10m[49m uninitialized read, leaving it to the code generator makes the byte-identical
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     65[0m:[38;5;10m[49m property depend on the optimization level.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     66[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m After the rewrite the Rust `.text` for all four functions is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m instruction-for-instruction identical to the C's (same opcodes and lengths; only
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m rip-relative displacements and PLT slot addresses differ), and both profiles pass
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the whole suite. `driver`'s `mov eax, 0` before each call and the trailing `nop`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m in every function are included for the same reason: with a stale pointer aimed
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     72[0m:[38;5;10m[49m into the library's own text, the instruction stream is itself part of the output.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     73[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     74[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Also confirmed as load-bearing and left in place:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `build.rs` passing `-Wl,-z,lazy` — the C reaches `good`/`bad`/`printLine`/`puts`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   through lazily-bound PLT slots, so the first call from `driver` runs
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `_dl_runtime_resolve`, which overwrites the very word `bad` is about to read.
